    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "overview",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Research Question\n\nThe main task is to use each stock's valuation at the end of the quarter, Scale and Growth Factors, Cross-sectional ranking predicting next quarter's earnings, Then convert the rankingTop30stock selection strategy. The additional question uses single-stock daily data to predict future direction., And convert probability into dynamic position. "
      },
      {
        "id": "coverage",
        "type": "markdown",
        "sourceId": "quality_source",
        "body": "## Data and Time Split\n\nMain sample contains39,616stock item-Quarterly Record, 4,281Only stock, 10quarter, Coverage2020-03-31to2022-06-30. By Time Before7Season training, after3Seasonal Test, Not randomly upset. Financial factors are first converted to quarterly cross-sectional percentiles., To reduce the impact of extreme values and dimensional differences. "
      },
      {
        "id": "main_method",
        "type": "markdown",
        "sourceId": "main_run_source",
        "body": "## Main Study: From Features to Portfolio Decisions\n\n1. X: 19Quarterly ranking of original financial factors for items4a composite factor.   \n2. Y: The regression model predicts next quarter's return ranking.; Logistic regression predicts whether it is higher than the median of the current season..   \n3. model: Linear regression, Ridge, Logistic Regression, Decision tree, Random forest and gradient boosting.   \n4. Decision-making: Sorted by prediction score in descending order each quarter, Master Strategy Equal Right to Buy Before30only.   \n5. Cost: Net income=Gross earnings-Unilateral20bpxTurnover rate. "
      },
