      {
        "id": "definitions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Metric Glossary\n\n- Rank IC: Predicted ranking and actual return rankingSpearmancorrelation coefficient. \n- AUC: Randomly selecting one rising sample and one falling sample., Probability of the model ranking upward samples first. \n- Turnover rate: Half the sum of absolute changes in weights across two adjacent periods; The initial position is recorded100%. \n- Maximum Drawdown: The maximum drawdown from the historical peak to the subsequent low of net value.. \n- Sharpe Ratio: Average excess return is obtained for each unit of volatility undertaken., This assignment assumes a risk-free rate of0. "
      }
    ]
